    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0794" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72115/3237</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-29T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your cipher telegram of December 27, 11 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d633-f1"/>
                    Department in its telegram of December 18, 4 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d633-f2"
                    /> expressed favorable opinion of proposal to deport enemy subjects from China
                    and intern in Australia. Does your present inquiry refer to same suggestion or
                    are enemy subjects to be deported to other places than Australia? Please fully
                    explain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
